{"c":[{"id":"9e24a23e53332473","sum":"A14-A15: fill asks once per form per 30 s and refocus posts no focus event: focus another field, start 40 s after the reader; empty a filled form before memory-negative checks; host hello settings override the helper's; watches fall back to the drawn field.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"11d6b8ce1c2c781d","sum":"A14 fill scripts: the helper asks about a form at most once per 30 s and refocusing a focused field posts nothing; focus another field first, start 40 s after the reader. A form the run filled is a source for the next: empty it before a memory-negative check.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T223314Z-9d4eecfc20a632d3","text":"On-screen fill scripts: the helper asks about a form at most once per 30 s (helper.ts FILL_REPEAT_MS) and refocusing an already-focused field posts no focus change; focus another field first and start 40 s after the reader (A14 memory_fill_walk.py).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T223314Z-ab5b060c9c18fb41","text":"A form the run filled is a window source for the next form: a memory-negative check must empty it first, or Jev may offer its values 'from Caret Fixture, Claim form' (A14 walk-3).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d418e99a3c6ab50e","sum":"A15: the host sends its gate settings on hello, overriding the helper's; socket walks needing Eager send 'settings set level eager' to the host. Line watches fall back to their drawn field when a focused-frame read fails; surface.lineHidden names the cover.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T010257Z-b452bfae15d1e4dd","text":"A host connected to the helper sends its own gate settings on hello (B10), overriding the helper's constructor settings: a socket walk that needs Eager (routine offers after 3 sightings) sends 'settings set level eager' to the host (A15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T010304Z-b5e36ef6f1a1befa","text":"Grammarly's ring is forgiven only against a frame: a failed focused-frame AX read (busy TextEdit) made the line watch hide Esc's stopped line as covered; watches now fall back to the field they were drawn for (A15). surface.lineHidden names the cover.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7b1fc1dbafe65231","sum":"A15-T1: Put back on Tab sends edit {onItsOwn:false} (refused until the helper takes it); Permissions lists skills by 'wrote'; VM display file is 2x pixels (3840x2400); close forms 3 s after a routine; compare field values by .utf16 or digest.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6e4afdbaf89e6e2d","sum":"A15-A16: 'Put back on Tab' sends memoryRequest edit {onItsOwn:false}, refused until the helper takes it; Permissions lists a skill under each write rule in its 'wrote', else only where skillRunsUnasked (skills.ts mayRunUnasked) allows now.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T010304Z-bc4f6fa45fbfa3dd","text":"B19 helper takes only {name} in a skill memoryRequest edit; host 'Put back on Tab' sends edit {onItsOwn:false} (host contract, Fixtures/memory.ndjson last line) and gets a refusal until the screen track adds it (A15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T030748Z-24aae3b87b1574fd","text":"Permissions page lists a skill under each write rule in its fields' 'wrote' (host contract; B19 helper stores wrote but strips it from replies); without it a skill is listed only where PermissionPolicy.skillRunsUnasked (mirrors skills.ts mayRunUnasked) allows now (A16).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c5a426b91e722cb8","sum":"A16-T1: rig VM display file is pixels at 2x (use 3840x2400 for panels beside forms); close fixture forms 3 s after a routine run; Swift String == is canonical equivalence, so field-value guards compare .utf16 or digests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T162636Z-ec02bde9a2237805","text":"Rig VM display file is pixels at 2x: 1920x1200 gives a 960x600-pt screen, too small for Caret's panels beside caret-fixture forms; A16's drawn walk uses 3840x2400. Close fixture forms >=3 s after a routine run or the bundle loses a copy and scores a miss.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T170510Z-7982a134da3a9b97","text":"Swift String == is canonical equivalence (precomposed é equals e+U+0301): guards comparing field values must use .utf16.elementsEqual or digests, or a normalizing app passes a mismatched write (T1 RangeEdit.verify).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
